## 2026-08-10 — Long-running festivals are date ranges, not real recurrence
**Status:** DEFERRED (needs client input)
**Severity:** Low
**Area:** `src/features/schedule/CalendarClient.jsx`, importer

Eight published festivals span more than 13 days; two exceed 60. The source spreadsheet gave a
start and an end date and nothing about which days inside that window the event actually runs, so
Clover Market (May 17 – Oct 4) is stored as one continuous 140-day range when it is really a
market on selected Sundays.

Mitigated in the UI: multi-day festivals show "Runs May 17 – Oct 4" on their opening day and
"Ongoing · through Oct 4" on any later day, plus an "Ongoing" badge past 13 days. The label
deliberately never claims the festival "recurs", because that cannot be inferred from duration —
Fringe and Welcome America genuinely do run continuously.

Closing properly needs either a `schedule_note` field the client fills in ("Sundays, May–October")
or real `FestivalOccurrence` rows per date. The schema already supports the latter; nobody has the
actual dates yet.

